[ask_88baf0ee] done in 397.9s; estimate 746,963; usd 0.8696
Best estimate: 746,963 slice/day (80% model-based interval 336,898 to 1,656,150 slice/day), for City of Chicago residents eating pizza within the city across restaurants, delivery, takeout, and frozen/prepared at home, averaged over 2025. Four routes were combined at roughly equal weight (3 methods): a bottom-up sales route using 1,987 Pizza restaurants establishments, 658,548 USD per pizzeria per year benchmark sales, and 28.2 USD per pizza local price; a national pie-count route from 3,000,000,000 pizzas per year; and a Chicago-DMA frequency route using 5.66 pizza orders per month orders with 4 slices per eating occasion and 3 slices per eating occasion per occasion. Only these points are observed; slices per pie (8), restaurant share (0.75), benchmark ratio (0.75), coverage (0.85), Chicago population (2,700,000), US population (330,000,000), and the local index (1.1) are analyst assumptions. The interval reflects disagreement among methods, not demonstrated accuracy. The biggest risk is the slice-count and frequency conflict; a Chicago-specific consumption survey would most improve it.

Key assumptions (proposed by the analyst model, not observed; code samples each one between the bounds shown):
- a1 Chicago-to-US ratio of pizza eating-occasion frequency (dimensionless): 1.1 dimensionless, range 0.7714 to 1.543 (range widened by code); used by m3. Overturned by: A Chicago-specific intake survey showing per-capita pizza eating at or below the national average.
- a2 Average slices per whole pizza (Chicago mix of thin, deep-dish, chain and frozen): 8 slices per pizza, range 5.477 to 10.95 (range widened by code); used by m1, m3. Overturned by: A Chicago-specific distribution of pie sizes/styles sold showing a mean slice count outside [n]-[n].
- a3 Share of Chicago pizza consumption occurring through restaurants/delivery/takeout (vs grocery/frozen/homemade): 0.75 fraction, range 0.5196 to 1.039 (range widened by code); used by m1. Overturned by: Evidence that frozen/homemade pizza accounts for more than ~[n] of Chicago pizza occasions.
- a4 Ratio of average Chicago pizzeria annual sales to the Slice top-quartile benchmark ($[n]): 0.75 dimensionless, range 0.5 to 1; used by m1. Overturned by: Chicago-specific average pizzeria revenue data showing it at or above $[n]k/year.
- a5 Share of Chicago pizza restaurant sales captured by the [n] counted establishments (coverage of the establishment count): 0.85 fraction, range 0.5766 to 1.153 (range widened by code); used by m1. Overturned by: Evidence that non-pizzeria outlets sell a large share (>[n]) of Chicago restaurant pizza.
- a7 Chicago resident population (City of Chicago, 2025): 2,700,000 people, range 1,903,943 to 3,807,887 (range widened by code); used by m3, m4. Overturned by: A Census estimate placing the 2025 city population outside [n]-[n] million.
- a8 US resident population (2025): 330,000,000 people, range 233,238,076 to 466,476,152 (range widened by code); used by m3. Overturned by: A Census estimate placing the 2025 US population outside [n]-[n] million.
